# Data ellipses: stat_ellipse

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:giggly, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"}
  ])
```

## About this notebook

This notebook follows the examples on ggplot2's reference page for
[`stat_ellipse()`](https://ggplot2.tidyverse.org/reference/stat_ellipse.html), in the order the
page gives them. Each example shows ggplot2's code first and then Giggly's. An example Giggly
cannot draw yet keeps its ggplot2 code and names what it is waiting for, so the page is also a
list of what remains.

`stat_ellipse()` draws an ellipse around the points of each group, by the method of the `car`
package's `dataEllipse()`: by default the ellipse at the 95% level of a multivariate
t-distribution fitted to `x` and `y`, drawn as a path. `type = "norm"` fits a normal distribution
instead, and `type = "euclid"` draws a circle whose radius is `level`. Giggly has none of it yet.
The examples use R's `faithful`: how long each eruption of the Old Faithful geyser lasted, and
the wait until the next.

## An ellipse around the points

```r
ggplot(faithful, aes(waiting, eruptions)) +
  geom_point() +
  stat_ellipse()
```

Not in Giggly yet: the `faithful` dataset and `stat_ellipse()`.

## An ellipse for each group

```r
ggplot(faithful, aes(waiting, eruptions, color = eruptions > 3)) +
  geom_point() +
  stat_ellipse()
```

`eruptions > 3` parts the short eruptions from the long, and colouring by it also groups by it,
so each group gets an ellipse of its own.

Not in Giggly yet: the `faithful` dataset, `stat_ellipse()`, and an expression in a mapping, such as
`eruptions > 3`.

## Normal and t ellipses

```r
ggplot(faithful, aes(waiting, eruptions, color = eruptions > 3)) +
  geom_point() +
  stat_ellipse(type = "norm", linetype = 2) +
  stat_ellipse(type = "t")
```

Not in Giggly yet: the `faithful` dataset, `stat_ellipse()` and its `type` option, a fixed
`linetype`, and an expression in a mapping, such as `eruptions > 3`.

## A circle

```r
ggplot(faithful, aes(waiting, eruptions, color = eruptions > 3)) +
  geom_point() +
  stat_ellipse(type = "norm", linetype = 2) +
  stat_ellipse(type = "euclid", level = 3) +
  coord_fixed()
```

`type = "euclid"` draws a circle of radius 3 around each group's centre, which looks round only
because `coord_fixed()` gives a unit of `x` the same length on the page as a unit of `y`.

Not in Giggly yet: the `faithful` dataset, `stat_ellipse()` and its `type` and `level` options, a
fixed `linetype`, `coord_fixed()`, and an expression in a mapping, such as `eruptions > 3`.

## Filled ellipses

```r
ggplot(faithful, aes(waiting, eruptions, fill = eruptions > 3)) +
  stat_ellipse(geom = "polygon")
```

Not in Giggly yet: the `faithful` dataset, `stat_ellipse()` drawn as polygons, `geom_polygon()`, and
an expression in a mapping, such as `eruptions > 3`.